        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Means",
            "Way out"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "E0382",
              "used after move",
              "borrow or `clone()`"
            ],
            [
              "E0505",
              "moved while borrowed",
              "end the borrow first"
            ],
            [
              "E0507",
              "move out of borrow",
              "`mem::take()`, `Option::take()`"
            ],
            [
              "E0506",
              "assign while borrowed",
              "assignment kills a live ref"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Aliasing Errors",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Means",
            "Way out"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "E0499",
              "two `&mut` at once",
              "sequence or `split_at_mut`"
            ],
            [
              "E0502",
              "`&mut` while `&` live",
              "shorten the shared borrow"
            ],
            [
              "E0596",
              "binding not `mut`",
              "add `mut` / `&mut self`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lifetime Errors",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Means",
            "Way out"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "E0597",
              "does not live long enough",
              "hoist the declaration"
            ],
            [
              "E0515",
              "return ref to local",
              "return owned, or take a buffer"
            ],
            [
              "E0716",
              "temporary dropped",
              "bind it with `let` first"
            ],
            [
              "E0106",
              "missing lifetime specifier",
              "add `<'a>` or return owned"
            ],
            [
              "E0521",
              "borrowed data escapes",
              "`move` closure or `'static`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Classic Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "v.push(v.len());          // ok: two-phase borrow",
            "map.insert(k, map[&k2]);  // E0502: no two-phase here",
            "let x = map[&k2]; map.insert(k, x);  // fix"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "E0502 In One Sentence",
          "text": "Copy the small read value out of the collection before the mutation, and the shared borrow is dead by the time the `&mut` starts."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Which fix do you try first?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Shorten the borrow — move or delete the later use.",
            "Split the data — disjoint fields or `split_at_mut`.",
            "Copy the small value out of the borrow.",
            "Restructure the ownership; clone only as the last step."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Name The Broken Rule",
          "items": [
            "Either a referent died before its reference, or",
            "an exclusive borrow overlapped another borrow.",
            "Every one of these codes is one of those two."
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
